### ЭТАП 2.2 - Тестирование RBAC Fresh Role Check
### Test: Middleware uses fresh role from database, not JWT payload

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@phone = +996555100200

### 1. Request OTP for test user
# @name requestOTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}",
  "purpose": "LOGIN"
}

@challengeId = {{requestOTP.response.body.challengeId}}

### 2. Verify OTP and login
# Note: Get actual OTP code from database:
# SELECT code_hash FROM "OtpChallenge" WHERE id = '{{challengeId}}';
# Or use bcrypt to generate hash for known code

# For this test, you need to:
# 1. Get the actual OTP from database
# 2. Replace "123456" with the actual code
# 3. Execute this request

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/phone/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challengeId": "{{challengeId}}",
  "code": "123456"
}

### 3. Get current session
# Expected: User created with role=USER
# @name getSession1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session

### 4. Manual step: Update user role in database
# Execute SQL:
# UPDATE "User" SET role = 'MANAGER' WHERE phone = '+996555100200';

### 5. Get session again WITHOUT re-login
# Expected behavior:
# - JWT still contains old role=USER
# - API should return fresh role=MANAGER from database
# - This proves middleware fetches fresh data
# @name getSession2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session

### Expected response:
# {
#   "user": {
#     "role": "MANAGER",  <- Fresh from DB, not from JWT
#     ...
#   }
# }

### 6. Test protected endpoint (if exists)
# Example: If you have an endpoint that requires MANAGER role
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users
# Expected: 200 OK (allowed because fresh role=MANAGER)

### 7. Manual step: Downgrade user role
# Execute SQL:
# UPDATE "User" SET role = 'USER' WHERE phone = '+996555100200';

### 8. Try to access MANAGER endpoint again
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users
# Expected: 403 INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS (blocked because fresh role=USER)

### 9. Manual step: Suspend user
# Execute SQL:
# UPDATE "User" SET status = 'SUSPENDED' WHERE phone = '+996555100200';

### 10. Get session after suspension
# Expected: 403 ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session

### 11. Manual step: Delete user
# Execute SQL:
# DELETE FROM "User" WHERE phone = '+996555100200';

### 12. Get session after deletion
# Expected: 401 INVALID_TOKEN "Пользователь не найден"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session

### Test Summary:
# ✅ Middleware fetches fresh user data from database on every request
# ✅ JWT is used only for identity (userId), not for authorization (role/status)
# ✅ Role changes are applied immediately without re-login
# ✅ Status changes (SUSPENDED) are enforced immediately
# ✅ Deleted users cannot access protected endpoints even with valid JWT

### Cleanup:
# Execute SQL:
# DELETE FROM "OtpChallenge" WHERE phone = '+996555100200';
# DELETE FROM "User" WHERE phone = '+996555100200';
